---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { useTranslations } from '../i18n/ui';

const t = useTranslations('en');
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title={t.meta.terms.title}
  description={t.meta.terms.description}
  path="/terms/"
  heading="Terms of Use"
  updated="Last updated: July 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Subject and scope</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms of Use ("Terms") govern access to and use of the leviora.ai website (the
    "Site") operated by Leviora ("we"). By accessing the Site you accept these Terms. They
    cover the Site only; use of the Leviora platform itself is governed by a separate
    written agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Content and no offer</h2>
  <p>
    Site content — text, images, diagrams and demonstrations — is provided for general
    information about the Leviora platform. It does not constitute a contractual offer or
    a commitment; product capabilities, packages and timelines are finalized in a written
    agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    All rights to the software, designs, text, logos, graphics and other content on the
    Site belong to Leviora or its licensors. Content may not be copied, reproduced,
    distributed or processed without prior written permission, except for personal,
    non-commercial viewing. Reverse engineering the Site or attempting to breach its
    security is prohibited.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The Site and its content are provided "as is", without warranties of accuracy,
    completeness or fitness for a particular purpose. To the extent permitted by law, we
    are not liable for indirect, incidental or consequential damages arising from use of
    the Site, except in cases of our gross negligence or willful misconduct.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    The Site may contain links to third-party websites. We do not control and are not
    responsible for their content or privacy practices; a link does not imply endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. The current version is always available
    on this page, with the date of the last update shown above.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Türkiye. The courts and
    enforcement offices of Istanbul (Çağlayan) have jurisdiction over any dispute arising
    from these Terms. Contact: <a href="mailto:info@leviora.ai">info@leviora.ai</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
